{
  "id": "GHSA-qg7r-fjh2-wvx8",
  "aliases": [],
  "title": "Stored cross-site scripting in `wpautop()` allows an unauthenticated visitor to inject script",
  "summary": "An unauthenticated visitor can post a comment containing a KSES-legal element whose attribute value holds a newline. `wpautop()` treats that newline as a paragraph boundary and rewrites a `<p>` inside the element, ultimately resulting in a live event-handler attribute being rendered on the page.\r\n\r\nWordPress 7.1.1 has been released containing a fix for the vulnerability, and as a courtesy to users on older branches the fix has been backported to all branches back to 5.9.\r\n\r\nDiscovered and responsibly disclosed by [Rafie Muhammad](https://www.linkedin.com/in/rafiemuhammad/) (Awesome Motive, Inc.)",
  "published_at": "2026-09-18T17:58:59.000Z",
